Defer the cuObject initialization of Cloudian's aws-sdk-cpp fork (tag 1.11.893+rdma) from
process start to the first use by an S3 client.

The fork constructs a cuObject client in a static initializer, which creates a CUDA context and
initializes cuFile in every process of an executable linked against it, also for runs that do
not use S3 (e.g. "elbencho --version", file I/O benchmarks, service instances). That costs about
a second per process start, writes errors to the cuFile log when no cuObject config is present,
and aborts the process (an assertion in cuFile) when the GPU has no free memory for another
context, e.g. on a host shared with other GPU jobs. With this patch the same check runs when the
first S3 client is created or RDMA is queried/enabled, so only S3 runs pay for it.

Applied by external/prepare-external.sh to a fresh clone of the fork (AWS_PATCHES, set by
contrib/plugins/s3rdma_cloudian/plugin.mk). Apply it by hand when building the fork yourself.

diff --git a/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.cpp b/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.cpp
index 79be107c0..ef4f232ea 100644
--- a/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.cpp
+++ b/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.cpp
@@ -79,15 +79,25 @@ namespace RdmaObj
         return nullptr;
     }
 
-    const char* rdma_status = rdmaStatusCheck();
-
-    // Declared before local_rdmaobj so it's already initialized with its
-    // real value by the time createLocalRdmaObj() (local_rdmaobj's own
-    // initializer) reads it - same-TU dynamic initializers run in
-    // declaration order.
-    bool native_io = rdma_status != nullptr;
+    // Set by init(), i.e. on first use rather than at process start: constructing
+    // the cuObject client creates a CUDA context and initializes cuFile, which
+    // every process of the executable would otherwise pay for (and which aborts
+    // when the GPU has no memory left), also processes that never touch S3.
+    const char* rdma_status = nullptr;
+    bool native_io = true;
+
+    void init() {
+        static const bool initialized = []() {
+            rdma_status = rdmaStatusCheck();
+            native_io = rdma_status != nullptr;
+            return true;
+        }();
+        (void) initialized;
+    }
 
     static std::unique_ptr<CuObjClient> createLocalRdmaObj() {
+        init();
+
         if (native_io) {
             // RDMA isn't usable process-wide, so skip constructing (and,
             // since ~CuObjClient() deliberately skips the vendor
diff --git a/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.h b/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.h
index 8c52fd037..69611695e 100644
--- a/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.h
+++ b/generated/src/aws-cpp-sdk-s3/source/RdmaObj.h
@@ -23,5 +23,10 @@ namespace RdmaObj
     extern thread_local std::unique_ptr<CuObjClient> local_rdmaobj;
     extern bool native_io;
 
+    // Initializes cuObject (rdmaobj, rdma_status, native_io) on first use.
+    // Called by everything that reads them, so that the CUDA context and the
+    // cuFile setup only happen in processes that create an S3 client.
+    void init();
+
     cuObjMemoryType_t rdmaObjGetMemoryType(const void *ptr);
 }
